{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q416502","formula":"ClLiO₃","hill":"ClLiO3","elements":["Li","O","Cl"],"composition":{"O":3.0,"Cl":1.0,"Li":1.0},"names":{"en":"Lithium chlorate","ru":"Хлорат лития","uk":"Хлорат літію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Lithium chlorate is the inorganic chemical compound with the formula LiClO3. Like all chlorates, it is an oxidizer and may become unstable and possibly explosive if mixed with organic materials, reactive metal powders, or sulfur. It can be manufactured by the reaction of hot, concentrated lithium hydroxide with chlorine: 3 Cl2 + 6 LiOH → 5 LiCl + LiClO3 + 3 H2O Lithium chlorate has one of the highest solubilities in water for a chemical compound.","ru":"Хлорат лития — соль хлорноватой кислоты и лития с формулой LiClO3, бесцветное гигроскопическое вещество.","uk":"Хлорат літію — це літієва сіль хлоратної кислоти з формулою LiClO3. Як і багато хлоратів, є сильним окисником при підвищеній температурі."},"fame":16,"pubchemCid":23682463,"mass":90.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Li+].[O-]Cl(=O)=O","inchikey":"XQHAGELNRSUUGU-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"lithium chlorate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"23682463","atoms":5,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.512,"y":-0.911,"z":-0.027,"el":"O"},{"x":0.57,"y":0.661,"z":-0.026,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.515,"y":0.506,"z":-0.026,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.245,"y":2.372,"z":-0.025,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.326,"y":-2.627,"z":0.103,"el":"Li"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1.0],[1,2,1.0],[1,3,1.0]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q416502","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithium_chlorate","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org